{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks","id":942521,"title":"Archmage Hacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-02T23:10:47-07:00","id":942521,"title":"Archmage Hacks","content":"So, The Imperial Mysteries are likely to be achieved in one of my games soon. Most of it looks like it will largely be able to work as written, with a few minor adjustments. A couple of things seem like they're going to need more adjustment, though:<br /> <br /> 1) The Arcane Experience Cost for actually crossing the threshold. The normal process has you expending one Arcane Experience per roll during some parts of the process. Given that 2E experiences are worth more than a 1E Experience Point, should this be adjusted to one Arcane Beat per roll in 2E? Should it stay as one Arcane Experience? What about other things that cost Arcane Experience Points?<br /> <br /> 2) Imperial Spell Factors<br /> A) Potency seems easy enough - 2 points of potency per step instead of one, in addition to making the spell undispellable without Imperial Practices.<br /> B) Duration would have a basic level of One Day -&gt; Month -&gt; Year (or say, ten years instead?). Should Lasting be an option on there?<br /> C) Scale - this is the one I have a serious problem with. All of the scale factors listed in IM are less than what is achievable by merely Advanced Scale in 2E. Thoughts on an appropriate progression?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 08-03-2016, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T23:22:25-07:00","id":942524,"title":"","content":"One <i>very</i> easy hack is to just give them Advanced Factors by default.<br /> <br /> Then having 6 dots in an Arcana just gives you an Archmaster-tier attainment and extra Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T23:31:16-07:00","id":942528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=942524#post942524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One <i>very</i> easy hack is to just give them Advanced Factors by default.<br /> <br /> Then having 6 dots in an Arcana just gives you an Archmaster-tier attainment and extra Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gives me some interesting ideas. The Imperial Practices could even be made into attainments instead of separate practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T03:08:17-07:00","id":942601,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that IM is but around a mechanic that's mostly been excised from 2e: rituals as extended casting. I'd be interested in seeing what people come up with to address this. <br /> <br /> I'll comment on the rest later; right now, work calls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T03:57:57-07:00","id":942627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=942601#post942601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that IM is but around a mechanic that's mostly been excised from 2e: rituals as extended casting. I'd be interested in seeing what people come up with to address this.<br /> <br /> I'll comment on the rest later; right now, work calls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To overcome that part of it I'd just treat spells that use the imperial practices as ones that have to be cast at ritual time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T05:08:08-07:00","id":942642,"title":"","content":"That would make testing time an exception to the proposed all advance factors rules. Which is fine, but it's definitely something that needs to be considered. More on this later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T05:09:10-07:00","id":942645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=942642#post942642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More on this later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking forward to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:00:50-07:00","id":942741,"title":"","content":"First: I don't like just giving Advanced Spell Factors to archmasters for two reasons: first, it clovers all of those Utility Attainments that are built around \u201cuse Advanced Spell Factor X without the need to Reach\u201d. Second, as pointed out above, there are unintended consequences to doing so. As well, a Seeker is probably going to have quite a bit of extra room to work with within the existing Reach mechanics: remember that the more you exceed the spell's Arcana requirements, the more Reach you can use without risking Paradox. So even as is, an Archmaster will be pulling off Master-level spells just as effectively as a Master pulls off Adept-level to Initiate-level spells. If it ain't broke, don't fix it. <br /> <br /> As well, the shift from Mage to Archmaster means that all of your Arcana are either Imperial or Ruling: that is, none are Common or Inferior. This, too, has implications that should not be ignored. <br /> <br /> The way I'd handle Imperial Spell Factors would be this: spend an Arcane Beat on a spell factor, and that factor's dice penalty gets halved. On the downside, the spell is treated as if you used too much Reach even if you haven't; i.e., you always roll a Paradox pool, even if it's just a Chance Die. <i>And</i> you can't use Advanced Casting Time when enhancing a spell in this way. <br /> <br /> Imperial Practices work as written, too, but with \u201cit must be an extended action\u201d replaced by \u201cit cannot use Advanced Casting Time\u201d. <br /> <br /> The next issue involves Imperial Attainments. Where the one-dot Attainment lets you see the Supernal and the three-dot Attainment lets you summon a Supernal Being into the Phenomenal World, the six-dot Attainment lets you physically enter the Supernal World. You can conduct an Astral Sojourn while physically in the Supernal World,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:56:56-07:00","id":943113,"title":"","content":"Universal attainments to consider:<br /> <br /> Identify Quintessence - Archmasters of an arcana are able to intuit how the nature of that arcana applies to a desired effect in the Fallen World, predicting the required aspects and understanding to achieve the desired effect. They also know when they have witnessed such sorts of patterns when they learn from it.<br /> <br /> Resort to Golden Road --- This sounds more like a property of the archmaster template than part of the <br /> Create Chantry --- Arguably either a part of the template OR knowledge of the arcana.<br /> Yantra Schmantra --- Archmagi understand confluences of magic. When casting a spell, they can apply any number of Yantras. (Maybe they don't count any Yantras that are also quintessence against their Yantra limits.)<br /> (My old thread on supernal trump---buried somewhere on the old forums---could provide some ideas for specific examples.)<br /> <br /> For the most part, I'd suggest simply using the systems pulled in straight. However, there's Imperial Spell Factors to consider as well as the ritual spell differences.<br /> <br /> Fix Duration Spell Factors by making them big and still the same order of expansion as Advanced Duration Spell Factors. 'Twas a silly oversight. (You need a math-minded sort to review these sorts of things, guys.)<br /> <br /> <b>Imperial Casting Time:</b> An archmagus can cast breathtaking effects for an investment of appropriate time and effort. For each Yantra* used in a spell, a level of Imperial Casting Time may be applied to a casting. This allows extended casting rules be applied. Each level allows one further roll be made to cast the spell, cast as normal for a ritual casting, but applied together as an extended roll. (*Possibly for each quintessence, arcane experience, permanent willpower, mana or something else.)<br /> <br /> Appropriate Conditions may be added per the normal rules and the Storyteller is free to add reasonable options (and we are free to come up with Attainments that interact here, too) but all spells can benefit from a set of spell-specific additions. <br /> <br /> * Reduced cost - Spell costs 1 less mana, willpower, or Arcane Experience<br /> * Faster Caster - Further casting rolls take half the casting time<br /> * Task Juggler - Caster may hold the imago crafting for a scene before starting the next roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> You also have Excision, even if the rules otherwise remain the same. Removing the limit of yantras one is allowed on a spell might simply be an attainment. Of course, Yantra could be unlimited while Quintessences replace them as the limited factor. If not, though, that's something for an archmage to update. The maximum benefit of Yantra could be raised to Gnosis or removed.<br /> Those would work wonders for raising the roof.<br /> <br /> Quintessence <i>could</i> be limited in quantity as per Yantra but have no limit on benefit, automatically, while Yantras simply work as they normally do. Quintessences could provide free Reach and dice, actually, and that would offset a lot of penalties. <br /> <br /> My <b>favorite</b> approach would be to rule that a single Quintessence applies to a single spell. (though a Prime attainment should allow fudging that by merging multiple) Yantras apply as normal, but do so first; each way in which a Quintessence applies as a valid Yantra applies a single bonus die, over and above the Yantra limit, and a bonus Reach. If any aspect of the Quintessence is used as one of the Yantra, that Yantra slot is used up and the full Yantra bonus dice are used instead of a single bonus die in the Quintessence bonus calculation, and is <i>not</i> factored into the net Yantra bonus. <br /> <br /> Thus, finding the perfect, most appropriate Quintessence is part of the casting mechanics and Yantra rules, both. This thing, I like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:01:36-07:00","id":943253,"title":"","content":"I put out some hacks to Imperial Mysteries for 2e shortly after it came out, though it likely could use tweaking. If you're interested though, you can find it here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kIDr9_-oBGLEPwmfmtTyTefnSh9d5D62LdY1fCa7UHI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Imperial Mysteries Patch</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:10:31-07:00","id":943371,"title":"","content":"Hey, Falco: You want feedback on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T23:28:59-07:00","id":943442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=943253#post943253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I put out some hacks to Imperial Mysteries for 2e shortly after it came out, though it likely could use tweaking. If you're interested though, you can find it here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kIDr9_-oBGLEPwmfmtTyTefnSh9d5D62LdY1fCa7UHI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Imperial Mysteries Patch</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I really, really like the way this is set up.<br /> <br /> My only concern is the invalidation of attainments like Everywhere and Time in a Bottle when becoming an Archmaster. A simple (to me, at least) fix seems to be allowing those attainments to step the factors up from Advanced to Imperial. Does that break anything in your opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T23:57:53-07:00","id":943460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=943442#post943442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really, really like the way this is set up.<br /> <br /> My only concern is the invalidation of attainments like Everywhere and Time in a Bottle when becoming an Archmaster. A simple (to me, at least) fix seems to be allowing those attainments to step the factors up from Advanced to Imperial. Does that break anything in your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never considered Time in a Bottle to be invalidated. I don't consider Instant casting to be an &quot;Advanced Factor&quot;, so much as just another use of Reach. I'll clarify that.<br /> <br /> As for Everywhere and Permanence, though, I'll put something in to that effect, that attainments like that allow Archmaster factors, so long as ritual casting time is used as normal. I don't think that breaks anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=943371#post943371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Falco: You want feedback on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>So long as it's constructive, sure, I'm generally open to feedback on my homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T00:08:47-07:00","id":943463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=943442#post943442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really, really like the way this is set up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, OTOH, think that it's overpowered and overkill. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=943442#post943442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only concern is the invalidation of attainments like Everywhere and Time in a Bottle when becoming an Archmaster. A simple (to me, at least) fix seems to be allowing those attainments to step the factors up from Advanced to Imperial. Does that break anything in your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have M1e available anymore; but IIRC, the relationship between common Spell Factors and Imperial Spell Factors is that the latter has each regular step the equivalent of two steps on the former. Thus my suggestion to have the skill penalties halved. <br /> <br /> I originally considered what you outline here; the problem is that that ends up spending one mana to do what's needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T00:27:30-07:00","id":943470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=943463#post943463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, OTOH, think that it's overpowered and overkill.<br /> <br /> I don't have M1e available anymore; but IIRC, the relationship between common Spell Factors and Imperial Spell Factors is that the latter has each regular step the equivalent of two steps on the former. Thus my suggestion to have the skill penalties halved.<br /> <br /> I originally considered what you outline here; the problem is that that ends up spending one mana to do what's needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, thankfully it's easy enough to ignore the free Advanced factors. Depends on how potent you want Archmages to be. I personally like the idea of stepping up the factors even for non-Imperial Arcana simply because Archmages are that much closer to the Supernal to start with. But YMMV.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, imperial factors were in 1e a little more complicated than just being 2 steps, having different multiples but the same starting point, or skipping some steps but not others, etc, but it'd still be pretty close that way, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-04-2016, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:26:08-07:00","id":943641,"title":"","content":"IMHO, the fact that every Arcanum that isn't Imperial is Ruling <i>already</i> addresses the fact that archmasters are \u201cthat much closer to the Supernal\u201d. Heck, consider the implications that single change has for Mage Sight and Supernal Summons: Travelers interact with the Supernal World based on their Paths' symbology and their Ruling Arcana (e.g., Mastigos see Space and Mind as a Labyrinth and Chains; and they sense and summon Space/Mind Supernal Entities, as Imps and Wraiths). A Seeker, with ten Ruling-or-better Arcana, probably can see and summon <i>all</i> Supernal Entities, and sees them in a manner consistent with his Lustrum \u2014 which may or may not resemble the symbology of his former Path, depending on what ordeal he goes through during his Threshold Seeking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T07:53:29-07:00","id":944315,"title":"","content":"Nevermind, I see that you answered my question already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:14:24-07:00","id":966232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=943253#post943253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I put out some hacks to Imperial Mysteries for 2e shortly after it came out, though it likely could use tweaking. If you're interested though, you can find it here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kIDr9_-oBGLEPwmfmtTyTefnSh9d5D62LdY1fCa7UHI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Imperial Mysteries Patch</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Next question: In your rules, can you use Reach for Imperial Factors if you don't have Archmastery in the Arcanum? Can a Mage with Time 8 use Imperial Potency for a Prime spell if they only have Prime 4?<br /> <br /> What about spending the Arcane Beat for <b>all </b>Imperial Factors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:31:03-07:00","id":966241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=966232#post966232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next question: In your rules, can you use Reach for Imperial Factors if you don't have Archmastery in the Arcanum? Can a Mage with Time 8 use Imperial Potency for a Prime spell if they only have Prime 4?<br /> <br /> What about spending the Arcane Beat for <b>all </b>Imperial Factors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah you can, just like atchmages could make any common spells, even if not at archmastery, use arcane factors with an arcane xp in 1e","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:43:20-07:00","id":966253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=966241#post966241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah you can, just like atchmages could make any common spells, even if not at archmastery, use arcane factors with an arcane xp in 1e</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing that prompted this question was a re-reading of Imperial Mysteries. Although the section on Enhancing Common Practices doesn't mention it, this is listed under the Archmaster Template section on page 27:<br /> <br /> &quot;An archmaster may spend one Arcane Experience to use the Imperial Spell Factor tables for the primary spell factor of an extended-action spell of the common Practices, as long as he has achieved archmastery in the primary Arcanum used.&quot;<br /> <br /> I wasn't sure if the lack of that bit was intentional or an oversight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:06:16-07:00","id":966296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=966253#post966253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that prompted this question was a re-reading of Imperial Mysteries. Although the section on Enhancing Common Practices doesn't mention it, this is listed under the Archmaster Template section on page 27:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;An archmaster may spend one Arcane Experience to use the Imperial Spell Factor tables for the primary spell factor of an extended-action spell of the common Practices, as long as he has achieved archmastery in the primary Arcanum used.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I wasn't sure if the lack of that bit was intentional or an oversight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah I actually missed that. Guess Ill tweak to match when I get home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T19:32:34-07:00","id":966539,"title":"","content":"Alright I made a slight tweak, to more match with the intent of 1e. Now you only get the free factor upgrades for arcana you have archmastery in, and similarly can only spend reach or beats to gain archmaster factors with those arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T01:28:06-07:00","id":966675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=966539#post966539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright I made a slight tweak, to more match with the intent of 1e. Now you only get the free factor upgrades for arcana you have archmastery in, and similarly can only spend reach or beats to gain archmaster factors with those arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing to potentially keep in mind - spell factors were much more tied to your arcana level in 1E. You had to have Arcana +1 to use prolonged, sensory etc. In 2E, it's all about reach - being a mage lets you use Advanced Factors for anything, provided you're willing to Reach for it.<br /> <br /> Archmages being able to use Imperial Factors for anything if they're willing to reach for it is just as flavorful, in my opinion. If the previous way you had it seems to out of touch with the intent of IM, another option would be to give the free factor upgrades only for Arcana you have Archmastery in, but still allow you to reach twice for Advanced + Imperial in something you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:50:38-07:00","id":969196,"title":"","content":"Interesting patch, I must say. Only I have some few questions to it - What does rules on Chantries mean here?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Chantries use the rules as provided in Imperial Mysteries, but instead of providing a universal 2 dice bonus to the Arcanum, it instead increases the locational Yantra that a Demesne would provide by 2 dice.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> Location Yantra in Demense have +2 bonus, so Chantry gives you bonus +4 to spellcasting instead? Does this also means that Chantries are treated as Demenses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T14:43:00-07:00","id":969464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=966675#post966675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to potentially keep in mind - spell factors were much more tied to your arcana level in 1E. You had to have Arcana +1 to use prolonged, sensory etc. In 2E, it's all about reach - being a mage lets you use Advanced Factors for anything, provided you're willing to Reach for it.<br /> <br /> Archmages being able to use Imperial Factors for anything if they're willing to reach for it is just as flavorful, in my opinion. If the previous way you had it seems to out of touch with the intent of IM, another option would be to give the free factor upgrades only for Arcana you have Archmastery in, but still allow you to reach twice for Advanced + Imperial in something you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree in some ways, but I was trying to stick close to the Source for that, as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942521-archmage-hacks?p=969196#post969196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting patch, I must say. Only I have some few questions to it - What does rules on Chantries mean here?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Chantries use the rules as provided in Imperial Mysteries, but instead of providing a universal 2 dice bonus to the Arcanum, it instead increases the locational Yantra that a Demesne would provide by 2 dice.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> Location Yantra in Demense have +2 bonus, so Chantry gives you bonus +4 to spellcasting instead? Does this also means that Chantries are treated as Demenses?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's in reference to this part of Imperial Mysteries:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every Chantry counts as a Demesne of the Realm to<br /> which the archmage\u2019s Road leads. In addition, spells of the<br /> Arcanum used to build the Chantry are cast with a 2 dice<br /> bonus. </div> </div> </div>So, yes, it still acts as a Demesne, like it mentions in the 1e book, but instead of providing the +2 dice it enhances the locational yantra to +4, yes. The main difference there is that it's subject to Yantra limitations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}